<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3791a648bdf0cf1eadb611f5cbd887923b5c0a1e98607fe3585e107bbf60641c</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--b38376dc9663.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ef5c69ec2e24fb5b0da414bbfe02c0fad7b27babb0284b2a319281861714b35</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--a133d5f50599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Explosive devices found near power plant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfacc3dd92ab34a8698bbd295f0a3b5d6e836288fc999012592a191c24c9bb6b</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741--1f323d2ba311.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police say they found unconventional explosive and incendiary devices near the Jänschwalde power plant in Brandenburg. Meanwhile, Germany's top diplomat says Algeria could become an important supplier of gas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Summer was 2nd hottest of the century — DWD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7259211e6d769b4d079c1275c88b3f30a2d442f4a0ad840663f614aae43035d0</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-summer-was-2nd-hottest-of-the-century-dwd/live-78568957--ff2313dd3357.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-summer-was-2nd-hottest-of-the-century-dwd/live-78568957?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's DWD weather service says the summer was second only to 2003 in terms of average temperatures. It was also unusually dry. In Cologne, police are seeking a man who fired shots at a cafe storefront.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany terminates lease for Berlin's Russian House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:163987a6baa05fddf5ed607dc459310550c89df0265818a2fa6609b902659643</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945--d12ecc0cddcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has announced the termination of the lease for the Russian House in the heart of Berlin. Critics have long said it is a hub for propaganda and espionage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's center-left SPD is fighting for survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1218ac0909b6431ab84465b2fb817445d6979180cc87319e22919666b1ffb403</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-center-left-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448--87d767b7a99e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-center-left-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Social Democratic Party is sinking ever deeper into crisis. Voters are turning away, while unrest is growing within its grassroots ranks. Will upcoming state elections accelerate the party's downward spiral?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ulrich Siegmund wants to make Saxony-Anhalt a model for AfD rule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c323999fdf20f27828cdf3900895df3a7d1ad1ac5a847e1ca70debeed54706c</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ulrich-siegmund-wants-to-make-saxony-anhalt-a-model-for-afd-rule/a-78579499--ccc2f807f9a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ulrich-siegmund-wants-to-make-saxony-anhalt-a-model-for-afd-rule/a-78579499?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD's lead candidate Ulrich Siegmund aims to turn his small federal state into a blueprint for right-wing extremist politics across Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--d7968a32f7c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92c2db82dae4a4580ce0ad6671f3326ef7b9f59bff909dbcfa0c52487272de87</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--3ab5f0359b92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ea5c43f16912fc8d07b404b180c35c27c0bd22aca18731970cfbc678a785db0</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--c7c332adab8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala collapses on pitch again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b19dc0e7e6bc7b223f5f12948161ae53cf04adc59aca288e39e58c2614a5e7c2</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:34Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T10:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021--4f3678c0bd32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of Germany's top footballers has collapsed on the pitch for a second time in four days ahead of the new season. Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala has said he has a "neurological dysfunction" that causes blackouts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
